# Citation metadata for perfora, in Citation File Format.
# https://citation-file-format.github.io
#
# GitHub reads this file and offers a ready-made citation in the sidebar
# ("Cite this repository"), in APA and BibTeX.
#
# TODO before the first public release:
#   * add `orcid:` to the author entry (https://orcid.org/…),
#   * add `affiliation:`,
#   * archive a tagged release on Zenodo and add the resulting `doi:` here,
#   * once a paper describing the method exists, add it as
#     `preferred-citation:` so citations point at the paper while this file
#     still credits the software itself.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use perfora in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "perfora: digitizing player-piano rolls into a reversible, millimetre-based model"
abstract: >-
  perfora turns scans and videos of player-piano rolls into structured,
  reversible data: every perforation as a note positioned in millimetres, and
  every printed or handwritten label with its position and scope. Lane spacing is
  measured from the roll rather than assumed, so unknown roll standards are
  handled without configuration, and uncertain results are recorded for review
  rather than discarded.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Alexander
    family-names: Vollmer
    email: alexander.vollmer.95@hotmail.de
repository-code: "https://github.com/perfora-project/Perfora"
url: "https://perfora.readthedocs.io"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
keywords:
  - player piano
  - piano roll
  - music roll
  - digitization
  - digital humanities
  - musicology
  - music information retrieval
  - optical music recognition
  - cultural heritage
